WEBVTT

1
00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:26.909
A STORY BASED ON REAL EVENTS

2
00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:07.079
THE SILENT HOUSE

3
00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:44.515
He hasn't arrived yet.

4
00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:53.234
It's so neglected here.

5
00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:12.875
Better to start with the grass at the back
and work towards the front.

6
00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:48.716
- What are you doing?
- Just looking.

7
00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:23.076
Wilson, how are you?

8
00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:26.272
- Sorry for the delay.
- It's okay. How are you?

9
00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:30.837
Fine. It's been so long. 
As I said, I want to sell the house-

10
00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:35.112
- But first I have to tidy it all up. Have you seen it?
- Yes.

11
00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:40.314
I told my daughter to get up early, to take advantage of the day.

12
00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:43.637
- I brought some water and blankets.
- Laura!

13
00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:48.319
- How are things in the village?
- Nothing changes.

14
00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:53.156
One realizes time passes when we see our kids.

15
00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:55.840
You're planning on selling?

16
00:06:55.960 --> 00:06:58.520
Yes. I live in the city now-

17
00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:02.758
- And my brother and I want to sell off all our properties around here.

18
00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:06.039
We won't be seeing you around anymore?

19
00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:09.675
I'll always come back. Memories, you know what I mean.

20
00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:16.670
- Have you been waiting long?
- No, we just arrived.

21
00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:19.990
Ok. Let's go inside.

22
00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:51.836
Here's another lamp, Laura.

23
00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:54.599
Wilson, come with me.

24
00:07:57.560 --> 00:08:02.634
It's worse than I thought. 
It's even worse upstairs.

25
00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:06.469
Loose tiles everywhere. It's dangerous. Don't go up.

26
00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:08.875
Come through here.

27
00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:18.470
Come on, Wilson.

28
00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:25.713
There are some candles here.

29
00:08:32.560 --> 00:08:36.394
- Here are some sofas. Will you be ok?
- Perfectly fine.

30
00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:39.956
We can manage everywhere. Don't worry.

31
00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:47.960
How much time will you need?

32
00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:52.153
I was thinking two or three days. If the weather's good.

33
00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:55.352
We thought we'd start from the back,

34
00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:57.948
go around, and finish up in front.

35
00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:01.675
- Do you agree?
- Of course. You're the expert.

36
00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:05.076
- Ok, that's our plan.
- By the way ...

37
00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:07.634
Come have a look.

38
00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:12.875
This door ...

39
00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:17.989
will be very useful for access to the front.

40
00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:20.031
Okay.

41
00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:22.720
Fine.

42
00:09:22.840 --> 00:09:26.150
Here are the keys. I'll be back with food later on.

43
00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:29.829
- No, don't worry.
- It doesn't bother me.

44
00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:31.712
I'll show you out.

45
00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:36.152
- Anyone interested?
- It's a matter of weeks.

46
00:09:36.280 --> 00:09:39.670
Negotiations have already been going on for a while.

47
00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:15.833
Laura, I'll leave you this.

48
00:15:47.600 --> 00:15:49.830
Dad!

49
00:15:49.960 --> 00:15:52.838
- Did you hear that?
- What!

50
00:15:52.960 --> 00:15:54.678
That noise.

51
00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:58.236
- What noise?
- There's somebody outside.

52
00:15:58.360 --> 00:16:01.557
There's no one, Laura. Go back to sleep.

53
00:17:45.680 --> 00:17:48.240
Dad, wake up!

54
00:17:48.360 --> 00:17:50.920
Did you not hear that?

55
00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:53.873
- What!
- Those noises again.

56
00:17:55.520 --> 00:17:58.273
Upstairs, Dad, please.

57
00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:01.476


58
00:18:02.360 --> 00:18:05.669
Ok. Here's what we'll do.

59
00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:09.833
I'll go up and look.

60
00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:14.512
But when I come down,
I want you to be asleep. Ok?

61
00:22:37.240 --> 00:22:39.356
Dad!

62
00:22:39.480 --> 00:22:41.596
Dad!

63
00:22:46.600 --> 00:22:48.636
What happened to you?

64
00:22:58.560 --> 00:23:00.755
Wake up, Dad.

65
00:23:03.960 --> 00:23:06.076
Wake up.

66
00:42:26.440 --> 00:42:28.556
What happened?

67
00:42:28.680 --> 00:42:30.910
Calm down.

68
00:42:31.800 --> 00:42:34.917
What did they do? What happened?

69
00:42:35.040 --> 00:42:37.349
What happened?

70
00:42:40.520 --> 00:42:42.875
Calm down.
What happened.

71
00:42:43.000 --> 00:42:45.070
Tell me what's going on.

72
00:42:45.600 --> 00:42:49.149
- We were attacked.
- Who?

73
00:42:49.280 --> 00:42:51.430
I don't know.

74
00:42:54.640 --> 00:42:57.950
- No, don't go!
- Stop it.

75
00:42:58.080 --> 00:43:00.878
I'll have a look.

76
00:43:01.000 --> 00:43:05.471
- Where's your father? Where is he?
- I don't know.

77
00:43:05.600 --> 00:43:10.230
- Let's find him.
- I don't want to go.

78
00:43:19.640 --> 00:43:21.710
I don't want to go.

79
00:43:25.920 --> 00:43:28.070
No, don't go.

80
00:43:28.200 --> 00:43:32.034
- Wait here, I'll have a look.
- Please... don't go.

81
00:44:10.800 --> 00:44:13.109
- Come on!
- I don't want to go.

82
00:44:13.240 --> 00:44:17.631
It's more dangerous here. There's nobody.

83
00:44:17.760 --> 00:44:20.911
There's nobody! Come on.

84
00:44:21.040 --> 00:44:23.110
Come on.

85
00:44:45.160 --> 00:44:47.674
Did you move the furniture?

86
00:45:13.280 --> 00:45:16.158
- Nestor. Nestor!
- stay there!

87
00:45:18.280 --> 00:45:20.555
Wilson!

88
00:46:00.920 --> 00:46:02.990
Put that down.

89
00:46:03.120 --> 00:46:04.872
Laura ...

90
00:46:05.960 --> 00:46:07.951
Where's your father?

91
00:46:08.080 --> 00:46:10.275
I don't know.

92
00:46:10.400 --> 00:46:13.312
Where did they attack you?

93
00:46:14.320 --> 00:46:16.788
Upstairs.

94
00:46:16.920 --> 00:46:20.115
You went upstairs...

95
00:46:27.200 --> 00:46:30.033
Wilson! Wilson!

96
00:47:13.920 --> 00:47:16.070
Keep calm.

97
00:47:52.720 --> 00:47:54.995
Here.

98
00:48:22.240 --> 00:48:24.390
Stay there.

99
00:48:42.360 --> 00:48:45.158
I told you not to go upstairs.

100
00:49:00.240 --> 00:49:02.629
Why did you go up?

101
00:49:22.440 --> 00:49:24.476
Dad!

102
00:49:24.600 --> 00:49:26.795
Dad!

103
00:49:26.920 --> 00:49:29.354
He isn't here.

104
00:49:34.240 --> 00:49:36.629
He isn't here, Laura.

105
00:49:40.520 --> 00:49:43.910
No one's been upstairs in a while.

106
00:49:54.000 --> 00:49:57.310
Let's go, Laura. He isn't here.

107
00:50:11.720 --> 00:50:13.597
Nestor?

108
00:50:14.760 --> 00:50:16.955
Nestor!

109
01:01:40.560 --> 01:01:42.516
Nestor!

110
01:01:42.640 --> 01:01:44.756
Nestor!

111
01:01:46.960 --> 01:01:49.599
What did they do to you?

112
01:03:24.000 --> 01:03:26.036
Are you okay?

113
01:03:27.240 --> 01:03:29.196
What happened?

114
01:03:29.320 --> 01:03:32.596
Who attacked you? Look at me.

115
01:03:36.920 --> 01:03:39.070
Nestor...

116
01:03:39.200 --> 01:03:42.272
What's going on in this house?

117
01:03:47.960 --> 01:03:50.349
Why, Laura?

118
01:03:50.960 --> 01:03:53.076
Why?

119
01:03:56.680 --> 01:03:59.274
I saw the pictures.

120
01:03:59.720 --> 01:04:02.757
- Which pictures?
- The photographs.

121
01:04:03.440 --> 01:04:06.876
- What are you talking about?
- The photographs in your room!

122
01:04:09.200 --> 01:04:11.509
Photographs!

123
01:04:11.640 --> 01:04:14.108
What are you saying, Laura?

124
01:04:20.520 --> 01:04:22.636
Do you miss her?

125
01:04:24.520 --> 01:04:27.353
- Who?
- Her.

126
01:04:28.320 --> 01:04:31.676
- Who?
- Our daughter. Do you miss her?

127
01:04:33.640 --> 01:04:36.950
- Tell her. She's there.
- I miss you.

128
01:04:37.080 --> 01:04:39.116
You're lying!

129
01:04:47.120 --> 01:04:49.190
Do you love me?

130
01:04:52.240 --> 01:04:54.435
Do you?

131
01:05:09.400 --> 01:05:11.914
Why didn't you come?

132
01:05:12.520 --> 01:05:15.080
I've been waiting for you.

133
01:05:16.560 --> 01:05:18.869
I'm here with you.

134
01:05:20.360 --> 01:05:22.749
I'm here.

135
01:05:24.360 --> 01:05:26.316
Help me.

136
01:05:27.360 --> 01:05:29.555
Shut up!

137
01:05:31.800 --> 01:05:33.950
Laura...

138
01:05:34.600 --> 01:05:39.435
I called your father because I wanted to see you. That's why I called him.

139
01:05:40.440 --> 01:05:43.955
- I needed to see you.
- Shut up!

140
01:05:44.080 --> 01:05:46.913
- Don't you remember?
- Shut up!

141
01:05:47.040 --> 01:05:50.589
Do you remember ... we agreed to talk it over.

142
01:05:50.720 --> 01:05:55.555
You knew we could not keep her.

143
01:05:55.680 --> 01:05:59.753
What have you done to your father? Did you kill him, Laura?

144
01:05:59.880 --> 01:06:03.998
- I told you to shut up!
- He knew this was for the best ...

145
01:06:04.120 --> 01:06:06.315
Listen...

146
01:06:06.440 --> 01:06:08.874
Shut up!

147
01:06:12.360 --> 01:06:15.272
You lied to me!

148
01:06:16.040 --> 01:06:19.191
He lied to me like you did...

149
01:06:19.320 --> 01:06:21.914
You killed my baby!

150
01:06:23.000 --> 01:06:25.833
You're going to die like my dad!

151
01:09:40.120 --> 01:09:42.236
Smile...

152
01:09:42.360 --> 01:09:44.430
Smile!

153
01:11:00.960 --> 01:11:04.635
Six days later, the mutilated bodies were found

154
01:11:04.760 --> 01:11:08.355
next to disturbing Polaroid photos.

155
01:11:08.480 --> 01:11:13.031
Despite the amount of evidence, the police investigation was inconclusive.

156
01:11:13.160 --> 01:11:15.958
The case was closed eight months later.

157
01:11:16.080 --> 01:11:20.517
Laura was never found.

158
01:16:04.800 --> 01:16:07.394
Sofi!

159
01:16:09.800 --> 01:16:11.791
Sofi!

160
01:16:19.360 --> 01:16:22.158
How lovely!

161
01:16:22.280 --> 01:16:24.191
- Were you playing?
- Yes.

162
01:16:24.320 --> 01:16:27.312
Shall we visit grandma?

163
01:16:27.440 --> 01:16:30.796
It's been a long time since we saw her.

164
01:16:31.440 --> 01:16:33.590
We're going to ride horses

165
01:16:33.720 --> 01:16:36.029
- And eat caramel.

166
01:16:37.720 --> 01:16:40.109
Let's go this way.

167
01:16:40.240 --> 01:16:42.390
And we're going to swim.

168
01:16:42.520 --> 01:16:44.636
Do you feel like swimming?

169
01:16:44.760 --> 01:16:47.399
Because Grandma has a canoe.

170
01:16:48.480 --> 01:16:51.074
It's like a little boat.

171
01:16:51.200 --> 01:16:54.158
You know what a canoe is? No?

172
01:16:54.280 --> 01:16:58.353
It's a really tiny boat.

173
01:16:58.480 --> 01:17:00.436
with room for...
all three of us,

174
01:17:00.560 --> 01:17:03.199
you, grandmother and I.

175
01:17:03.320 --> 01:17:05.470
And the doll can go too.

176
01:17:06.000 --> 01:17:09.754
You know Grandma's looking
forward to meeting you?

177
01:17:09.880 --> 01:17:12.917
But she lives far away...

178
01:17:13.040 --> 01:17:16.191
We have to walk
and walk and walk...

179
01:17:17.920 --> 01:17:19.990
And there ...

180
01:17:20.120 --> 01:17:22.588
We can see...

181
01:17:26.320 --> 01:17:29.437
a lot of sun.

182
01:17:33.760 --> 01:17:35.990
in the countryside.

183
01:17:37.400 --> 01:17:39.436
What do you say?

184
01:17:39.560 --> 01:17:41.755
No.

185
01:17:50.440 --> 01:17:53.591
Or don't you feel like walking?

186
01:17:56.680 --> 01:17:59.148
Sofi, I love you so much.

187
01:18:01.800 --> 01:18:04.519
You know there's
a little house in a tree.

188
01:18:04.640 --> 01:18:09.111
When I was a little girl,
I used to play there everyday.

189
01:18:09.240 --> 01:18:11.515
You can use it too.

190
01:18:12.600 --> 01:18:17.433
- It's near the lake.
- You know that lake?

191
01:19:06.240 --> 01:19:11.109


192
01:22:00.760 --> 01:22:03.718
